Not in the current version of NetHack, indeed.

However, the distribution of items is now fixed per dungeon branch (for
example, the Mines generate more tools, gehennom more wands, etc.).

This could, arbitrarily, also be made dependant on character class.

The Dev Team could use this to make the various classes more varied: for
example, a wizard could be made to get more wands and scrolls, while
priests and healers could get more potions. Fighter classes could get
more weapons and armour, etc. This would make the game easier, and
characters would be less dependant on a good starting inventory.

On the other hand, the chances could also be tweaked in exactly the
opposite direction: wizards would get more weapons and armour randomly
generated, healers and priests would get more weapons and less potions,
and fighters would get more wands. This would make the game harder, and
characters would be encouraged to make good use of their starting
inventories.

Both generation schemes would in some way encourage roleplaying and
increase the difference between classes.

